%S A400538 1,99,621,1935,4409,8411,14309,22471,33265,47059,64221,85119,110121,
%T A400538 139595,173909,213431,258529,309571,366925,430959,502041,580539,
%U A400538 666821,761255,864209,976051,1097149,1227871,1368585,1519659,1681461,1854359,2038721,2234915,2443309
%N A400538 Number of lattice points of the truncated tetrahedron whose vertices are the permutations of (+-n, +-n, +-3n) with an even number of minus signs.
%C A400538 The truncated tetrahedron is obtained by cutting off the corners of the regular tetrahedron with vertices (3n,3n,3n), (3n,-3n,-3n), (-3n,3n,-3n) and (-3n,-3n,3n) at one third of each edge. It is the set of points (x,y,z) with x+y+z, x-y-z, -x+y-z and -x-y+z at most 5n, and -x-y-z, -x+y+z, x-y+z and x+y-z at most 3n.
%C A400538 For n >= 1, it has (184*n^3 - 84*n^2 + 26*n - 3)/3 interior lattice points and 56*n^2 + 2 boundary lattice points.
%H A400538 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400538/b400538.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400538 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/TruncatedTetrahedron.html">Truncated Tetrahedron</a>.
%H A400538 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (4,-6,4,-1).
%F A400538 a(n) = (184*n^3 + 84*n^2 + 26*n + 3)/3.
%F A400538 G.f.: (1 + 95*x + 231*x^2 + 41*x^3)/(1 - x)^4.
%F A400538 E.g.f.: exp(x)*(3 + 294*x + 636*x^2 + 184*x^3)/3.
%F A400538 a(n) = 4*a(n-1) - 6*a(n-2) + 4*a(n-3) - a(n-4) for n >= 4.
%e A400538 For n = 1 the truncated tetrahedron has 99 lattice points, of which 41 are interior and 58 are on the boundary.
%t A400538 A400538[n_] := 2*n*(n*(92*n + 42) + 13)/3 + 1;
%t A400538 Array[A400538, 35, 0] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 09 2026 *)
%o A400538 (PARI) a(n) = (184*n^3 + 84*n^2 + 26*n + 3)/3
%o A400538 (Python) def a(n): return (184*n**3 + 84*n**2 + 26*n + 3)//3
%Y A400538 Compare A371532 (cuboctahedron) and A371515 (truncated octahedron).
